## Findings
1. blocking — brief:48 [severity: S1] The limit "malformed, empty or non-string ids are rejected upstream" is false for an absent id: `petitio.opus` is optional (schema `opusId?: string`, adapters/native/src/index.ts:510 passes `data.opus` through, check.ts:740 only checks a present `opus`), and 7 of the real studio's 22 petitiones (P-001, P-020 and others, qa-lead retro asks) carry none. The prototype's `needsYouTotal` puts `petitio.opus` into one Set, so every open unlinked `needs_you` petitio collapses into a single `undefined` member: three open retro asks with no opus show "Inbox 1" in the shell and in the Inbox refresh callback, where today's `petitiones.length` shows 3. No existing or planned row catches it, because W-345-b6 is migrated onto the same helper and the only orphan fixture (`W-404`) is linked. Replacement text: "limit: malformed, empty or non-string ids are rejected upstream by `petitio.opus`; an open petitio with no `opus` link is its own work item and counts once under its petitio id (`needsYouTotal` keys it `petitio:<id>`), creates no Board card, and is pinned by `W-409-b2` "two unlinked open petitiones count two"; cross-studio identity and closed petitiones are unclassified." Add the matching Input domain row after brief:67. [design: keeps] [class: spec×input-domain-missing-or-unenforceable] — check: apps/web/test/w409.test.ts W-409-b2 "two unlinked open petitiones count two"
2. advisory — brief:114 [severity: S4] Sense: the shared total renders as the badge on the Inbox nav item ("Inbox 2" on board-sample-1280-expanded.png), but greenlight asks are a Board verb (DIRECTION §8) and the Inbox screen lists only petitiones. In the real studio, 38 opera are `backlog` today, so the badge will read about 38 or more while the Inbox screen says "Nothing waiting on you", and Needs you will never be "empty on a good day". The sample captures, which have one backlog opus, do not show this. Default 2 says "the shell" and does not say that the Inbox badge will count Board-only asks or how large the count gets. Replacement text for Default 2: "The Inbox nav badge will count distinct work items across Board greenlights, human gates and Inbox questions. In this studio that is about 38 backlog opera plus open asks, while the Inbox screen still lists only questions. Agree, or should the badge count only Inbox questions (by distinct opus) and leave greenlights to the Board's Needs-you column?" [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: none: a served row asserting the Inbox badge equals what the Inbox screen offers, or the Patron's ruling recorded in DIRECTION §6
3. advisory — brief:30 [severity: S2] "no Inbox screen markup or interaction changes" leaves out a reported-status change. `Inbox.tsx:237` derives `empty` from `data.opera.length` as well as `data.petitiones.length`. Once backlog opera are widened into `opera`, a studio with any backlog opus and no open petitio reports `ready` rather than `empty` to the shell's `role="status"` region, while InboxView still shows "Nothing waiting on you". Replacement text: "`apps/web/src/screens/Inbox.tsx`: report the same unique-opus total after refresh; no Inbox screen markup or interaction changes; limit: the screen's reported status stays derived from the widened `opera` membership, so a backlog-only studio reports ready, not empty (reused, not promised)." [class: spec×fix-opens-new-surface] — check: none: a w341-style row asserting Inbox status is `empty` when `petitiones` is empty and `opera` holds only backlog entries

## Verdict
One blocking S1 that keeps the design: `needsYouTotal` merges every open petitio with no opus link into one count, and the brief's limit wrongly says upstream rejects that input. It is a required fix in the build, together with its b2 assertion and domain row. The Inbox-badge sense question and the status wording are advisory.
VERDICT: FAIL
